# The founder's review is required on these paths once "Require review from Code Owners" is on in the ruleset of main
# and claude/build-platform (docs/runbooks/github-governance.md, step 5; docs/adr/0063). Every owner named here is a
# GitHub login on packages/db/domain-model/approvers.json (tools/test/codeowners.test.ts).

# Every path, first (the founder's ruling of 2026-10-20): every pull request needs the founder's own approval, so the
# one required approval cannot come from another account with Write, such as the build agent's on a Dependabot pull
# request. GitHub takes the last line that matches a path, so each line below names the founder again for what it
# protects.
* @PureTideWater

# The schema and its approval.
/packages/db/migrations/ @PureTideWater
/docs/product/domain-model.md @PureTideWater
/packages/db/domain-model/ @PureTideWater
# The generated function files: each migration's changes to a function, read as diffs beside the document
# (docs/adr/0068).
/packages/db/functions/ @PureTideWater

# The code that decides an approval: a pull request could otherwise pass the gate by changing its judge.
/packages/db/src/domain-model/ @PureTideWater
/packages/db/src/cli/domain-model.ts @PureTideWater
/tools/approval-of-record/ @PureTideWater

# The code that decides whether the gate runs at all: which migrations apply (migrate.ts), the catalog test, which
# tests run and what each script does (vitest.config.ts, the package.json files), the fixture guard the hooks call,
# and the release immutability check. A pull request could otherwise leave the gate's judge alone and stop it running.
/packages/db/src/migrate.ts @PureTideWater
/packages/db/src/cli/migrate.ts @PureTideWater
/packages/db/src/catalog.ts @PureTideWater
/vitest.config.ts @PureTideWater
/package.json @PureTideWater
/packages/db/package.json @PureTideWater
/packages/synth/src/guard/ @PureTideWater
/tools/check-releases-immutable.sh @PureTideWater

# The engine freeze (reconciliation-001; docs/adr/0064): its check, its differential test and the exception a pull
# request declares in exception.json, so declaring one takes the founder's review.
/tools/engine-freeze/ @PureTideWater

# The switch that decides which model features a real provider serves in production (docs/adr/0070, Part 2): the
# committed baseline, the reports each entry is recomputed from, the recall and precision floors and the confirmed
# prices; and the code that judges them, which decides serving from them (evaluated.ts), parses them (baseline-format.ts,
# floors-format.ts) and records or refuses an entry (eval/baseline.ts, eval/floors.ts). A pull request could otherwise
# leave the switch's data alone and serve a feature by changing its judge.
/packages/model-gateway/eval/baseline.json @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/eval/floors.json @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/eval/reports/ @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/config/models.json @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/src/evaluated.ts @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/src/baseline-format.ts @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/src/floors-format.ts @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/eval/baseline.ts @PureTideWater
/packages/model-gateway/eval/floors.ts @PureTideWater

# The published rule releases (content/releases is created by publish-content.yml) and the synthetic releases.
/content/releases/ @PureTideWater
/fixtures/synthetic/rules/release-*/ @PureTideWater

# The rules every session and every workflow runs under.
/CLAUDE.md @PureTideWater
/.claude/ @PureTideWater
/.github/ @PureTideWater
